my react component keeps re-fetching forever and the tab freezes, also get this warning in console. what am i doing wrong?? ive been on this for 2 hours
Warning: Maximum update depth exceeded. This can happen when a component calls setState inside useEffect, but useEffect either doesn't have a dependency array, or one of the dependencies changes on every render.
    at OrderList (OrderList.jsx:9)
heres the code
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
export default function OrderList({ customerId }) {
  const [orders, setOrders] = useState([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
  const filters = { status: 'open', customerId };
  useEffect(() => {
    setLoading(true);
    fetch(`/api/orders?status=${filters.status}&customer=${filters.customerId}`)
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(data => {
        setOrders(data.items);
        setLoading(false);
      });
  }, [filters]);
  if (loading) return <p>Loading...</p>;
  return (
    <ul>
      {orders.map(o => <li>{o.id} - {o.total}</li>)}
    </ul>
  );
}
also there's another warning about keys but idk if thats related. the api itself works fine when i call it in postman, returns like 12 items. i tried removing the dependency array completely and it got even worse lol. this is for a small internal dashboard at work, im mostly a backend person so hooks still confuse me

stm32f103, reading a 10k NTC through a voltage divider on PA1 w/ the ADC. value jumps around like crazy (±80 counts) and is also about 5% too low vs my multimeter. code:
uint16_t read_adc(void) {
    HAL_ADC_Start(&hadc1);
    HAL_ADC_PollForConversion(&hadc1, 10);
    return HAL_ADC_GetValue(&hadc1);
}
float adc_to_volts(uint16_t raw) {
    return raw * 3.3f / 4096.0f;
}
sampling time is set to 1.5 cycles in cubemx, divider is 10k fixed + the NTC, no cap on the pin. vdda measures 3.28V. is it my code or my circuit or both

